Date: Wed, 22 Jul 2026 00:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dpu: enable 8bpc dither on AYN Odin 3

The tested Odin 3 display path uses 8-bpc output, so the existing DPU helper
disables output dithering. Enable the same static ordered dither matrix for
8-bpc output on this machine only. Keep temporal dithering disabled and
preserve the existing 6-bpc and disable paths everywhere else.

This isolated downstream change makes no RGB101010, panel descriptor, DSI, or
DSC changes. It is not a claim that every 8-bpc panel should enable DPU
dithering.

Signed-off-by: enjihn <150061999+enjihn@users.noreply.github.com>
---
NOTE (linux-handheld-aarch64): the message above is enjihn's, unchanged. The
diff below is NOT their original file — it is the same change, regenerated with
three lines of context.

Their patch is a zero-context (-U0) diff, which carries line numbers and nothing
to match them against, so `patch` cannot tell a correct insertion point from a
shifted one and would silently put `case 8:` in the wrong place after any edit
above it in this file. patches/0010-msm-resource-cleanup.patch edits the same
file, so that is not hypothetical. With context, a shift is found by content or
refused outright.

Regenerated from their patch applied to 7.2.1 + the full series; verified
identical in effect. Original: enjihn/armada-packages
kernel/patches/0011-drm-msm-dpu-enable-8bpc-dither-on-ayn-odin3.patch at
ee7c31c6fba444423e64fa12be370dc57fa014f7, sha256
f56266556535d3e8f28643232db779f7f68de55a00cb36b86a1ecf166816ab56.

 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.c
@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@
 #define pr_fmt(fmt)	"[drm:%s:%d] " fmt, __func__, __LINE__
 #include <linux/debugfs.h>
 #include <linux/kthread.h>
+#include <linux/of.h>
 #include <linux/seq_file.h>
 
 #include <drm/drm_atomic.h>
@@ -401,6 +402,17 @@
 		dither_cfg.c3_bitdepth = 6;
 		dither_cfg.temporal_en = 0;
 		break;
+	case 8:
+		if (!of_machine_is_compatible("ayn,odin3")) {
+			hw_pp->ops.setup_dither(hw_pp, NULL);
+			return;
+		}
+		dither_cfg.c0_bitdepth = 8;
+		dither_cfg.c1_bitdepth = 8;
+		dither_cfg.c2_bitdepth = 8;
+		dither_cfg.c3_bitdepth = 8;
+		dither_cfg.temporal_en = 0;
+		break;
 	default:
 		hw_pp->ops.setup_dither(hw_pp, NULL);
 		return;
